# The release key's public half goes here, one line, as
#
#   releases@getmarula.com ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3Nza...the-public-key...
#
# It is the trust anchor for two things: verifying a signed release tag in a
# clean clone, and verifying the signature over a release's SHA256SUMS with
# `ssh-keygen -Y verify` or `marula artifact verify`.
#
# It is deliberately empty in the repository. A committed placeholder key is a
# key somebody is told to trust and nobody holds, so the signing job refuses to
# publish until a real line is added here. RELEASING.md carries the command that
# produces it.
#
# Rotation: add the new line, keep the old one for one release so artifacts
# signed before the rotation still verify, then remove it.
